From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: L33TEST Crossroads <dullclarity@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 09:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] multizorkd: never log verbatim input for credential-bearing
 prompts

process_connection_command() logs every raw input line before dispatch:

    loginfo("New input from socket %d%s: '%s'", ..., conn->inputbuf);

Two input handlers receive a secret on that line:
  - inpfn_hello_sailor                  (returning-player access code)
  - inpfn_enter_instance_code_to_join   (game join code)

When the active handler is either of those, emit a fixed "<redacted>" marker
instead of the raw line. All other input is logged exactly as before. This is
unconditional (no config), touches only the log string, and makes no protocol,
schema, or gameplay change.
---
 multizorkd.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/multizorkd.c b/multizorkd.c
index c96a9f8..e050d83 100644
--- a/multizorkd.c
+++ b/multizorkd.c
@@ -2257,7 +2257,16 @@ static void process_connection_command(Connection *conn)
     sanitize_to_low_ascii(conn->inputbuf);
     trim(conn->inputbuf);
 
-    loginfo("New input from socket %d%s: '%s'", conn->sock, conn->blocked ? " (blocked)" : "", conn->inputbuf);
+    // Some input handlers receive a secret on this line: the returning-player
+    //  access code (inpfn_hello_sailor) and the game join code
+    //  (inpfn_enter_instance_code_to_join). Never write those verbatim to the
+    //  log; emit a fixed redaction marker instead. All other input is logged
+    //  unchanged.
+    if ((conn->inputfn == inpfn_hello_sailor) || (conn->inputfn == inpfn_enter_instance_code_to_join)) {
+        loginfo("New input from socket %d%s: <redacted>", conn->sock, conn->blocked ? " (blocked)" : "");
+    } else {
+        loginfo("New input from socket %d%s: '%s'", conn->sock, conn->blocked ? " (blocked)" : "", conn->inputbuf);
+    }
 
     if (conn->blocked) {
         return;  // don't process this input further.
